# `/data/*`, NOT `/data/` -- git does not descend into an excluded DIRECTORY, so a
# negation inside one is never even evaluated. Excluding the contents is what makes the
# exception below reachable.
/data/*
# ...except the deck snapshot, which is a COMMITTED build artefact rather than a download.
# [A107] The app boots from it instead of querying (7.51s -> 0.02s), so it has to ship with
# the code. Everything else in data/ is a 51 MB re-downloadable archive; this is 170 kB and
# is regenerated by `uv run python -m tools.snapshot_deck`.
!/data/deck_snapshot.json.gz
# [A182] The puzzle games' facts (Bingo and what follows). Same trap, same reason: a missing
# file does not break the site, it makes every puzzle route answer 503.
!/data/puzzle_facts.json.gz
.env
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.DS_Store

# local Claude Code settings
.claude/settings.local.json
.vercel
# [A248] Build a Career's phase leans, ~15 kB. Without it every career plays with no lean.
!/data/phase_skill.json.gz
# [A258] Career skills and season roles, ~26 kB. Without it no card shows a skill.
!/data/player_skills.json.gz
# [A259] The engine numbers before A259, frozen once, for past daily challenges.
!/data/engine_a160.json.gz
# [A267] A259's engine numbers, which the daily replays days from 2026-11-07 on
!/data/engine_a259.json.gz
# [A268] A260's batting leans, for a daily day before LEANS_CENTRED_FROM
!/data/leans_a260.json.gz
